Test the generator of IReal numbers, i.e. that generated values are
proper numbers (satisfy the Cauchy criterion) in the intended range.
    range is (0,10)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,1000)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,10^6)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,10^10)          +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test the generator of IReal intervals, i.e. that generated values are
proper intervals (the end points are proper numbers and left end point
smaller than right end point) and have midpoint in the intended range.
    range is (0,10)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,1000)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,10^6)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    range is (0,10^10)          +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test that function values are proper real numbers, i.e. function
values for random arguments satisfy Cauchy criterion.
   exp over (0,100)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sin over (0,100)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   log over (0,100)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   atan over (0,100)            +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test that function values for interval arguments are proper intervals,
i.e. the end points are proper numbers and left end point smaller
than right end point.
   exp over (0,10)              +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sin over (0,10)              +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   log . (+1) . abs over (1,10) +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   atan over (0,10)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test that randomly generated expression values are proper real numbers.
   range is (0,1)               +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   range is (0,5)               +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test that functions in Floating give consistent results in
instances for IReal and Double, i.e. differ in at most two
last bits of Double mantissa.
   log over (1,10^6)            +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sin over (0,pi)              +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   exp over (0,100)             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   atan over (0,10^6)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sqrt over (0,10^6)           +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test commutativity of addition  +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test commutativity of multiplication+++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test associativity of addition  +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test associativity of multiplication+++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test that the following functions are the identity function.
Use random inputs, uniformly distributed over given intervals.
True equality cannot be tested; test passes if |f(x) - x| < 1e-200.
   exp . log over (0,10)        +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   exp . log over (0,1000)      +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   exp . log over (0,10^10)     +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sq . sqrt over (0,10)        +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sq . sqrt over (0,1000)      +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   sq . sqrt over (0,10^10)     +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   tan . atan over (0,10)       +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   tan . atan over (0,1000)     +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   tan . atan over (0,10^10)    +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   asin . sin over (-1,1)       +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   asinh . sinh over (0,100)    +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
   recip . recip over (0,1000)  +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test pi, by testing the following identities up to 1e-200.
   sin pi = 0                   +++ OK, passed 1 test.
   cos pi = -1                  +++ OK, passed 1 test.
   atan 1 = pi/4                +++ OK, passed 1 test.
Test the following identities up to 1e-200, for random real numbers.
    cos x^2 + sin x^2 = 1       +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    sin (2*x) = 2*sin x*cos x   +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
Test the following identities up to 1e-200, for random non-zero numbers.
    log |x*y| = log |x|+log |y| +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
    x * recip x = 1             +++ OK, passed 100 tests.
